c/p\u003e\n\u003cp dir=\"auto\"\u003eSpecial search qualifiers can be provided in the full-text query:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eauthor:bcoe\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter results in which \u003ccode\u003ebcoe\u003c/code\u003e is the author\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003emaintainer:bcoe\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter results in which \u003ccode\u003ebcoe\u003c/code\u003e is qualifier as a maintainer\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003escope:foo\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter results published under the \u003ccode\u003e@foo\u003c/code\u003e scope\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ekeywords:batman\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter results that have \u003ccode\u003ebatman\u003c/code\u003e in the keywords\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eseparating multiple keywords with\n\u003cul dir=\"auto\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e,\u003c/code\u003e acts like a logical \u003ccode\u003eOR\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e+\u003c/code\u003e acts like a logical \u003ccode\u003eAND\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e,-\u003c/code\u003e can be used to exclude keywords\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003enot:unstable\u003c/code\u003e: Exclude packages whose version is \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt; 1.0.0\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003enot:insecure\u003c/code\u003e: Exclude packages that are insecure or have vulnerable dependencies (based on the \u003ca href=\"https://nodesecurity.io/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ensp\u003c/a\u003e registry)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eis:unstable\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter packages whose version is \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt; 1.0.0\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eis:insecure\u003c/code\u003e: Show/filter packages that are insecure or have vulnerable dependencies (based on the \u003ca href=\"https://nodesecurity.io/\" rel=\"nofollow\"\u003ensp\u003c/a\u003e registry)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eboost-exact:false\u003c/code\u003e: Do not boost exact matches, defaults to \u003ccode\u003etrue\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/article\u003e","richTextTruncated":false,"renderedFileInfo":null,"symbols":{"timed_out":false,"not_analyzed":false,"symbols":[{"name":"Public Registry API","fully_qualified_name":"Public Registry API","kind":"section_1","ident_start":2,"ident_end":21,"extent_start":0,"extent_end":7670,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":2},"end":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":21}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":0,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":213,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Table of Contents","fully_qualified_name":"Table of Contents","kind":"section_2","ident_start":26,"ident_end":43,"extent_start":23,"extent_end":508,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":20}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":2,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Objects","fully_qualified_name":"Objects","kind":"section_2","ident_start":511,"ident_end":518,"extent_start":508,"extent_end":2747,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":3},"end":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":10}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":20,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":71,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Registry","fully_qualified_name":"Registry","kind":"section_3","ident_start":524,"ident_end":532,"extent_start":520,"extent_end":838,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":22,"utf16_col":4},"end":{"line_number":22,"utf16_col":12}},"extent_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":22,"utf16_col":0},"end":{"line_number":36,"utf16_col":0}}},{"name":"Package","fully_qualified_name":"Package","kind":"section_3","ident_start":842,"ident_end":849,"extent_start":838,"extent_end":1531,"ident_utf16":{"start":{"line_number":36,"u